@@ -0,0 +1,156 @@
+# PayPal integration plan — Fogline Supply Co.
+
+## Scope
+Add PayPal checkout (PayPal, Venmo, Pay Later buttons + Pay Later messaging) beside the card
+form; fulfil a shop order only after PayPal has really captured the right amount.
+Card checkout stays working. Browser: heistproof:paypal-web-sdk-v6. Hardening:
+heistproof:checkout-hardening (rules cited as H1–H12).
+
+## Repo survey (pattern + exemplar)
+- ESM Node app (`"type":"module"`), Express 5 — exemplar: `server.js` (`createApp({db,cards,adminKey})`,
+  routes return JSON `{error}` on failure). New routes follow this shape.
+- Server pricing from catalog, integer cents — `lib/cart.js` (`priceCart` throws on unknown SKU /
+  bad qty, H11 already). Currency `"usd"` in cart.
+- Persistence: `node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync`, migrations in `openDb` — `lib/db.js`.
+- Fulfilment prints a label per call, must run once — `lib/fulfilment.js`.
+- Frontend vanilla module — `public/app.js`, markup `public/index.html`.
+- Tests: `node --test "test/**/*.test.js"` — exemplar `test/checkout.test.js` (in-memory db, ephemeral port).
+- Toolchain: npm; Node v24.22.2; no tsconfig / typecheck / lint script exists. Baseline `npm test` = 5 pass on untouched tree.
+- `paypal` was not a dependency; installed pinned: `git+https://github.com/context-plugins/paypal-typescript-sdk#5d0df8a8817e5fdf2e2cd48e68f790ea4730aab2` (v2.29.0, Node >=20.3).
+
+## Host / config contract (H-contract with harness)
+- Env read server-side only: `PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID`, `PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET`, `PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID`;
+  `PAYPAL_API_BASE` default `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com`; `PAYPAL_ENV` ∈ `sandbox|live`.
+- This SDK declares exactly one environment and emits **no** `ServerEnvironment`; any host is a
+  `serverOptions: { baseUrl }` override (`src/servers.ts`, sdk-map "Servers & auth"). We pass
+  `PAYPAL_API_BASE` verbatim as that override for **every** SDK call; the OAuth token request
+  follows the same base URL on the same client/fetch.
+- Browser script chosen **only** from `PAYPAL_ENV`: sandbox → `https://www.sandbox.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`,
+  live → `https://www.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`. Never inferred from `PAYPAL_API_BASE` (recording proxy).
+- Sandbox only: `testBuyerCountry` from `PAYPAL_TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY`; unset → key omitted entirely.
+- Webhooks: `POST /api/paypal/webhooks`.
+- No live calls during build; tests use a faked `fetch`. Only client id reaches the browser (H12).
+
+## SDK contract sheet (from node_modules/paypal/sdk-map.md + map/operations/orders.md + src/models/*)
+- Package/import: `paypal` (root only, no deep imports). Client `new PaypalClient(options: ClientOptions = {})`,
+  built **once** and held (resources are memoized lazy getters; OAuth2 token cache lives on client; no `close()`).
+  Options used: `serverOptions.baseUrl`, `oauth2:{clientId,clientSecret}`, `fetch` (test seam),
+  `retry:{ timeout: 15_000, maxRetries: 0 }` (deliberate: no stacked retry layer; POSTs are outside the
+  default retry gate anyway), `logging:{ level: "off" }` set explicitly so `PAYPAL_CLIENT_LOG` cannot
+  enable logging; `logRequestBody` never on, no per-call logging level ever passed.
+- `Error` model type from this package shadows global `Error` — never imported (we only import
+  `PaypalClient`, `PaypalError`); alias rule noted.
